│  1. **Sub-question (Definitional):** What foundational concepts,             │
│  taxonomies, and theoretical models define inter-agent communication         │
│  protocols and coordination frameworks in multi-agent systems (MAS)?         │
│     * **Keywords:** "agent communication protocol", "multi-agent             │
│  coordination framework", "cooperative game theory", "agent interaction      │
│  topology", "shared state space", "agent communication language"             │
│     * **Synonyms:** "inter-agent messaging standards", "collaborative agent  │
│  ontology"                                                                   │
│     * **Search angle:** Definition / Conceptual framework                    │
│                                                                              │
│  2. **Sub-question (Mechanism - Communication):** What specific              │
│  message-passing protocols, memory architectures, and structured prompt      │
│  formats enable direct information exchange and state synchronization among  │
│  LLM-based agents?                                                           │
│     * **Keywords:** "agent-to-agent message passing", "shared memory         │
│  blackboard architecture", "natural language negotiation", "speech act       │
│  theory", "structured communicative prompts", "context window                │
│  synchronization"                                                            │
│     * **Synonyms:** "inter-agent prompt passing", "verbal interaction        │
│  protocol"                                                                   │
│     * **Search angle:** Method description                                   │
│                                                                              │
│  3. **Sub-question (Mechanism - Coordination & Consensus):** How do          │
│  multi-agent systems execute dynamic task allocation, role assignment, and   │
│  consensus-building during joint planning and execution?                     │
│     * **Keywords:** "decentralized consensus protocol", "dynamic role        │
│  assignment", "hierarchical task decomposition", "contract net protocol",    │
│  "multi-agent debate mechanism", "majority voting consensus"                 │
│     * **Synonyms:** "distributed task negotiation", "agent workflow          │
│  orchestration"                                                              │
│     * **Search angle:** Method description                                   │
│                                                                              │
│  4. **Sub-question (Comparative):** How do centralized controller-driven     │
│  communication topologies compare to decentralized (peer-to-peer)            │
│  coordination architectures regarding latency, computational efficiency,     │
